Usage: col [OPTION]...

Filter reverse line feeds from standard input.

col filters out reverse (and half-reverse) line feeds so that the output
is in the correct order with only forward and half-forward line feeds.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

  -b    do not output backspaces
  -f    permit forward half line feeds
  -p    pass unknown control sequences
  -x    output spaces instead of tabs
  -l    buffer at least NUM lines (default 128)

OPTIONS:
  -b             do not output backspaces
  -f             permit forward half line feeds
  -p             pass unknown control sequences
  -x             output spaces instead of tabs
  -l ARG         buffer at least NUM lines (default 128)
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
